/**
@mainpage Jiminy Engine

A Python implementation of the **Jiminy Advisor**, a normative reasoning and
argumentation framework for **multi-stakeholder decision making**. Jiminy turns context
facts and normative rules into *explainable moral recommendations* by combining normative
systems, formal argumentation, stakeholder preferences and context-dependent reasoning.

@author Francisco J. Rodríguez-Lera (University of León)
@version 1.0

## Pipeline

```
Context Facts
  -> YAML Scenario Loader
  -> Norm Representation (body -> head, type, stakeholder)
  -> Argument Generation (normative detachment)
  -> Argumentation Framework (arguments + attacks)
  -> Semantics Evaluation (naive / grounded / preferred / stable / priority / jiminy)
  -> Accepted Arguments
  -> Moral Recommendations (deontic actions)
  -> Narrative Explanation
```

## Modules

- `jiminy/engine.py` — the `Jiminy` engine (semantics).
- `jiminy/norms.py` — the `Norm` rule representation.
- `jiminy/arguments.py` — the `Argument` representation.
- `jiminy/yaml_loader.py` — scenario loading.
- `jiminy/visualization/` — Graphviz visualizers.

## Reference

> Liao, B., Pardo, P., Slavkovik, M., & van der Torre, L. (2023).
> *The Jiminy Advisor: Moral Agreements among Stakeholders Based on Norms and Argumentation*.
> Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research (JAIR).
*/
